+{"created_at": "2026-07-01T17:46:49.843216+00:00", "ocr_backend": "sglang", "ocr_endpoint_version": "modal-sglang-unlimited-ocr-v1", "ocr_model": "Unlimited-OCR", "ocr_model_version": "Unlimited-OCR", "ocr_text": "<PAGE><|det|>header [71, 56, 194, 72]<|/det|>VLTS3-i3\n<|det|>title [71, 96, 909, 157]<|/det|>DIRECT THEFT OF SURPLUS BALANCE\nWHEN UNSTAKING STHYPE\n<|det|>text [72, 189, 210, 209]<|/det|>SEVERITY:\n<|det|>text [295, 190, 387, 208]<|/det|>Critical\n<|det|>text [72, 243, 152, 260]<|/det|>PATH:\n<|det|>text [71, 278, 644, 296]<|/det|>src/stHYPEWithdrawalModule.solutpdate#L431-L475\n<|det|>title [72, 317, 259, 337]<|/det|>REMEDIATION:\n<|det|>text [70, 352, 926, 432]<|/det|>It is not safe to make direct transfers to the pool if you are unsure whether current execution is inside of a swap callback. It should therefore be verified using the reentrancy switch of the Sovereign Pool, however this is currently not exposed.\n<|det|>text [70, 441, 926, 520]<|/det|>One possibility is to add a donate function to the SovereignPool that only works for rebase tokens (donations are possible with transfers already anyway) and has the nonReentrant modifier. That way you can safely donate the tokens back to the pool without the risk.\n<|det|>text [70, 530, 926, 590]<|/det|>If modifications to the SovereignPool are not possible, then dummy calls that check whether reverts happen due to reentrancy are needed. This is often used to guard against read-only reentrancy for Balancer or Curve.\n<|det|>title [72, 623, 182, 642]<|/det|>STATUS:\n<|det|>title [238, 624, 304, 641]<|/det|>Fixed\n<|det|>title [72, 676, 259, 695]<|/det|>DESCRIPTION:\n<|det|>text [70, 710, 920, 802]<|/det|>The stHYPE Withdrawal Module exposes functionality for the owner of the module to unstake stHYPE into HYPE using the Overseer contract. The owner calls unstakeToken0Reserves, which in turn transfers stHYPE from the SovereignPool (uses the STEXAMM) and then calls\n<|det|>text [70, 805, 920, 870]<|/det|>burnAndRedeemIfPossible to create a Burn request. The stHYPE is burned immediately and the Burn request can be redeemed later once filled for HYPE.\n<|det|>text [70, 884, 911, 951]<|/det|>In the update function, any received HYPE from redeemed Burn requests is first allocated to any outstanding LP withdrawal requests after which the surplus is deposited back into the Sovereign Pool directly on lines 471-474:\n<|det|>page_number [910, 956, 937, 970]<|/det|>13\n", "page_image_sha256": "18fe679a18d9ae4f4b6bea4c4fd3c520ca509db2b6f7d12fccdac265a20fd861", "page_number": 13, "pdf_id": "pdf_002911_39a2c2ee71c9", "raw_record": {"code_blocks": [], "confidence": null, "created_at": "2026-07-01T17:46:49.843216+00:00", "layout_blocks": [], "ocr_backend": "sglang", "ocr_endpoint_version": "modal-sglang-unlimited-ocr-v1", "ocr_model": "Unlimited-OCR", "ocr_model_version": "Unlimited-OCR", "ocr_settings": {"dpi": 300, "image_mode": "base", "mode": "pages", "ngram_size": 35, "ngram_window": 1024, "prompt": "Multi page parsing."}, "ocr_text": "<PAGE><|det|>header [71, 56, 194, 72]<|/det|>VLTS3-i3\n<|det|>title [71, 96, 909, 157]<|/det|>DIRECT THEFT OF SURPLUS BALANCE\nWHEN UNSTAKING STHYPE\n<|det|>text [72, 189, 210, 209]<|/det|>SEVERITY:\n<|det|>text [295, 190, 387, 208]<|/det|>Critical\n<|det|>text [72, 243, 152, 260]<|/det|>PATH:\n<|det|>text [71, 278, 644, 296]<|/det|>src/stHYPEWithdrawalModule.solutpdate#L431-L475\n<|det|>title [72, 317, 259, 337]<|/det|>REMEDIATION:\n<|det|>text [70, 352, 926, 432]<|/det|>It is not safe to make direct transfers to the pool if you are unsure whether current execution is inside of a swap callback. It should therefore be verified using the reentrancy switch of the Sovereign Pool, however this is currently not exposed.\n<|det|>text [70, 441, 926, 520]<|/det|>One possibility is to add a donate function to the SovereignPool that only works for rebase tokens (donations are possible with transfers already anyway) and has the nonReentrant modifier. That way you can safely donate the tokens back to the pool without the risk.\n<|det|>text [70, 530, 926, 590]<|/det|>If modifications to the SovereignPool are not possible, then dummy calls that check whether reverts happen due to reentrancy are needed. This is often used to guard against read-only reentrancy for Balancer or Curve.\n<|det|>title [72, 623, 182, 642]<|/det|>STATUS:\n<|det|>title [238, 624, 304, 641]<|/det|>Fixed\n<|det|>title [72, 676, 259, 695]<|/det|>DESCRIPTION:\n<|det|>text [70, 710, 920, 802]<|/det|>The stHYPE Withdrawal Module exposes functionality for the owner of the module to unstake stHYPE into HYPE using the Overseer contract. The owner calls unstakeToken0Reserves, which in turn transfers stHYPE from the SovereignPool (uses the STEXAMM) and then calls\n<|det|>text [70, 805, 920, 870]<|/det|>burnAndRedeemIfPossible to create a Burn request. The stHYPE is burned immediately and the Burn request can be redeemed later once filled for HYPE.\n<|det|>text [70, 884, 911, 951]<|/det|>In the update function, any received HYPE from redeemed Burn requests is first allocated to any outstanding LP withdrawal requests after which the surplus is deposited back into the Sovereign Pool directly on lines 471-474:\n<|det|>page_number [910, 956, 937, 970]<|/det|>13\n", "page_image_sha256": "18fe679a18d9ae4f4b6bea4c4fd3c520ca509db2b6f7d12fccdac265a20fd861", "page_number": 13, "pdf_id": "pdf_002911_39a2c2ee71c9", "raw_response_ref": "chunk_0028/other_audit_repo_pdfs/pdf_002911_39a2c2ee71c9_valantis-mar-25_Final/pages_0013_0016.raw.json", "source_abs_path": "/home/experiments_base/smart-contract-data/crawlers/output/repos/audit_repos/Smart-Contract-Review-Public-Reports/valantis-mar-25(Final).pdf", "source_bucket": "other_audit_repo_pdfs", "source_filename": "valantis-mar-25(Final).pdf", "source_page_count": 38, "source_pdf_sha256": "64bf545adb3699eed16cd21abb0d6db6a651ca273e2992a02122825ec61966a7", "source_rel_path": "Smart-Contract-Review-Public-Reports/valantis-mar-25