+{"created_at": "2026-07-01T17:46:49.843216+00:00", "ocr_backend": "sglang", "ocr_endpoint_version": "modal-sglang-unlimited-ocr-v1", "ocr_model": "Unlimited-OCR", "ocr_model_version": "Unlimited-OCR", "ocr_text": "<PAGE><|det|>header [72, 56, 186, 72]<|/det|>VLTS3-9\n<|det|>title [71, 97, 770, 190]<|/det|>WITHDRAWAL QUEUE PRIORITY\nBYPASS FOR FEELESS INSTANT\nWITHDRAWAL\n<|det|>text [72, 222, 204, 243]<|/det|>SEVERITY:\n<|det|>text [309, 223, 369, 243]<|/det|>High\n<|det|>title [72, 276, 259, 295]<|/det|>REMEDIATION:\n<|det|>text [71, 311, 926, 370]<|/det|>The creation of the LP withdrawal request should only take the order into account, e.g. by keeping a cumulative withdrawn amount that can then be used in claim to ensure that the claimer has the rights to the claimable ETH.\n<|det|>text [72, 403, 325, 425]<|/det|>STATUS: Fixed\n<|det|>title [72, 456, 259, 475]<|/det|>DESCRIPTION:\n<|det|>text [70, 490, 911, 557]<|/det|>When a Withdrawal is created, it references the cumulativeAmountToken1ClaimableLPWithdrawalCheckpoint pointer to track when a claim is allowed, according to the existing withdrawal queue.\n<|det|>text [118, 580, 725, 694]<|/det|>LPWithdrawals[idLPWithdrawal] = LPWithdrawalRequest({\n    recipient: _recipient,\n    amountToken1: amountToken1.toUint96(),\n    cumulativeAmountToken1ClaimableLPWithdrawalCheckpoint:\n    cumulativeAmountToken1ClaimableLPWithdrawal\n});\n<|det|>text [70, 719, 905, 833]<|/det|>However, cumulativeAmountToken1ClaimableLPWithdrawal only gets updated after a call to the update function and only if the HYPE was received from the Overseer. So any withdrawal request made after another one while it's not claimable yet are in the same queue at the same cumulative amount:\n<|det|>text [97, 857, 833, 936]<|/det|>if (address(this).balance <= amountToken1ClaimableLPWithdrawalCache) {\n    amountToken1ClaimableLPWithdrawal = address(this).balance;\n    return;\n}\n<|det|>page_number [911, 956, 935, 970]<|/det|>21\n", "page_image_sha256