+{"created_at": "2026-07-01T17:46:49.843216+00:00", "ocr_backend": "sglang", "ocr_endpoint_version": "modal-sglang-unlimited-ocr-v1", "ocr_model": "Unlimited-OCR", "ocr_model_version": "Unlimited-OCR", "ocr_text": "<PAGE><|det|>header [71, 56, 194, 72]<|/det|>VLTS3-14\n<|det|>title [71, 97, 877, 190]<|/det|>READ-ONLY REENTRANCY IN\nWITHDRAW CAN LEAD TO SWAP FEE\nMANIPULATION\n<|det|>text [73, 222, 207, 242]<|/det|>SEVERITY:\n<|det|>text [290, 223, 388, 242]<|/det|>Medium\n<|det|>text [72, 276, 152, 294]<|/det|>PATH:\n<|det|>text [71, 311, 496, 329]<|/det|>src/STEXAMM.sol:withdraw#L523-L624\n<|det|>title [72, 350, 259, 370]<|/det|>REMEDIATION:\n<|det|>text [70, 386, 878, 445]<|/det|>It is advisable to use a modifier for view function that are susceptible to read-only reentrancy. The modifier only checks whether the reentrancy guard is active and does not need to set it.\n<|det|>text [73, 477, 325, 498]<|/det|>STATUS: Fixed\n<|det|>title [72, 531, 259, 550]<|/det|>DESCRIPTION:\n<|det|>text [70, 565, 875, 657]<|/det|>In the withdraw function for LP shareholders in STEXAMM, the caller can choose to unwrap their wHYPE and receive native HYPE instead. This happens on lines 599-602 and an external call is made to the receiver, giving them execution.\n<|det|>text [70, 668, 918, 781]<|/det|>Even though the function itself has the nonReentrant modifier, it is still an intermediate state: the token0{stHYPE} has already been burned previously using burnToken0AfterWithdraw on line 589, while remaining token1{wHYPE} is yet to be taken out of the pool using withdrawLiquidity on line 611.\n<|det|>text [70, 795, 837, 888]<|/det|>Even though the pool itself does not use the token0/token1 ratio for valuation, it does use this ratio to calculate the swap fee in STEXRatioSwapFeeModule:getSwapFeeInBips, which is used in SovereignPool:swap.\n<|det|>page_number [907, 955, 941, 970]<|/det|>26\n", "page_image_sha256": "18722b210342973fa8e1ae2f6ca321656e55a7a82e66ba22e386c908d2d03d10", "page_number": 26, "pdf_id": "pdf_002911_39a2c2ee71c9", "raw_record": {"code_blocks": [], "confidence": null, "created_at": "2026-07-01T17:46:49.843216+00:00", "layout_blocks": [], "ocr_backend": "sglang", "ocr_endpoint_version": "modal-sglang-unlimited-ocr-v1", "ocr_model": "Unlimited-OCR", "ocr_model_version": "Unlimited-OCR", "ocr_settings": {"dpi": 300, "image_mode": "base", "mode": "pages", "ngram_size": 35, "ngram_window": 1024, "prompt": "Multi page parsing."}, "ocr_text": "<PAGE><|det|>header [71, 56, 194, 72]<|/det|>VLTS3-14\n<|det|>title [71, 97, 877, 190]<|/det|>READ-ONLY REENTRANCY IN\nWITHDRAW CAN LEAD TO SWAP FEE\nMANIPULATION\n<|det|>text [73, 222, 207, 242]<|/det|>SEVERITY:\n<|det|>text [290, 223, 388, 242]<|/det|>Medium\n<|det|>text [72, 276, 152, 294]<|/det|>PATH:\n<|det|>text [71, 311, 496, 329]<|/det|>src/STEXAMM.sol:withdraw#L523-L624\n<|det|>title [72, 350, 259, 370]<|/det|>REMEDIATION:\n<|det|>text [70, 386, 878, 445]<|/det|>It is advisable to use a modifier for view function that are susceptible to read-only reentrancy. The modifier only checks whether the reentrancy guard is active and does not need to set it.\n<|det|>text [73, 477, 325, 498]<|/det|>STATUS: Fixed\n<|det|>title [72, 531, 259, 550]<|/det|>DESCRIPTION:\n<|det|>text [70, 565, 875, 657]<|/det|>In the withdraw function for LP shareholders in STEXAMM, the caller can choose to unwrap their wHYPE and receive native HYPE instead. This happens on lines 599-602 and an external call is made to the receiver, giving them execution.\n<|det|>text [70, 668, 918, 781]<|/det|>Even though the function itself has the nonReentrant modifier, it is still an intermediate state: the token0{stHYPE} has already been burned previously using burnToken0AfterWithdraw on line 589, while remaining token1{wHYPE} is yet to be taken out of the pool using withdrawLiquidity on line 611.\n<|det|>text [70, 795, 837, 888]<|/det|>Even though the pool itself does not use the token0/token1 ratio for valuation, it does use thi